{
  "source": "video-audit/the-next-token-build-2026-10-09-v2/edited.wav",
  "duration": 201.1,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.02,
      "text": "AI builds an answer one token at a time."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.6,
      "end": 7.62,
      "text": "At each step, the model calculates probabilities for the tokens that could come next,"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.24,
      "end": 11.34,
      "text": "but AI doesn't always pick the highest probability token"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.34,
      "end": 15.6,
      "text": "to understand why we'll look at two things, sampling and temperature."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.36,
      "end": 19.04,
      "text": "Let's say you ask, what should I name my new dog?"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.68,
      "end": 22.42,
      "text": "The AI builds the reply up to a frozen context."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.02,
      "end": 26.86,
      "text": "You could name him, leaving a blank space for the very next choice."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.86,
      "end": 33.06,
      "text": "At this exact blank, the AI calculates a probability for every token in its vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.02,
      "end": 39.16,
      "text": "Because spot is the top choice at 22%, you might expect the AI to pick it every time."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.68,
      "end": 42.98,
      "text": "But having the best chance doesn't mean a 100% win rate."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.7,
      "end": 48.82,
      "text": "A 22% probability means AI would pick spot about 22 times out of 100 tries,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.14,
      "end": 50.96,
      "text": "on average, if the odds stay the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.62,
      "end": 52.48,
      "text": "That's called sampling."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.3,
      "end": 55.8,
      "text": "This chart shows exactly how this works in practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.8,
      "end": 61.6,
      "text": "We are going to keep the 22% probability for spot and all the other odds completely unchanged"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.6,
      "end": 66.44,
      "text": "to see how sampling plays out across five random picks for this same open token."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.28,
      "end": 73.56,
      "text": "These five random picks produce pick one, max, pick two, spot, pick three, buddy,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.02,
      "end": 76.46,
      "text": "pick four, recs and pick five, max."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.38,
      "end": 80.04,
      "text": "These are not five names in a row in a single sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.6,
      "end": 84.76,
      "text": "They are five separate parallel attempts at filling that exact same single blank."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.76,
      "end": 89.46,
      "text": "Notice that despite having the highest probability, spot was only picked once."
    },
    {
      "start": 90.28,
      "end": 92.64,
      "text": "Another set of five picks could turn out entirely differently."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.42,
      "end": 96.5,
      "text": "The highest statistical chance is not a strict guarantee."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.18,
      "end": 100.74,
      "text": "If an AI simply chose the most likely token every single time,"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.12,
      "end": 104.04,
      "text": "the resulting answers would become highly predictable and repetitive."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.94,
      "end": 108.84,
      "text": "Giving other likely tokens, like max or buddy, a chance to be selected,"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.92,
      "end": 111.48,
      "text": "introduces necessary variety into the responses."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.48,
      "end": 117.4,
      "text": "One slightly different token choice at a critical juncture can send the entire remainder"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.4,
      "end": 120.16,
      "text": "of the generated answer in a completely new direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.0,
      "end": 125.96,
      "text": "Temperature is the tool that changes how concentrated or spread out these probabilities are."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.72,
      "end": 129.02,
      "text": "In chat apps, it's already set for you behind the scenes."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.92,
      "end": 133.08,
      "text": "This table compares next token probabilities under different settings."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.04,
      "end": 138.28,
      "text": "Looking at the baseline odds calculated from the model's training and the frozen prompt context,"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.28,
      "end": 141.38,
      "text": "we see spot starts at 22%."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.38,
      "end": 143.5,
      "text": "Watch what happens when we lower the temperature."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.4,
      "end": 148.34,
      "text": "A lower temperature concentrates the odds heavily onto the most likely tokens."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.1,
      "end": 155.92,
      "text": "Spot's chance leaps from 22% to 36%, which effectively shrinks the chances for the less likely names."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.94,
      "end": 161.72,
      "text": "A higher temperature does the exact reverse, spreading the odds more widely across the vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.86,
      "end": 166.22,
      "text": "Here, spot's dominant chance falls to just 16%."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.22,
      "end": 170.46,
      "text": "This levels the playing field, giving less likely names a much better chance of being picked."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.1,
      "end": 177.64,
      "text": "A 22% baseline to start, up to 36% with low temperature and down to 16% with high temperature."
    },
    {
      "start": 178.62,
      "end": 180.84,
      "text": "These specific probabilities are illustrative."
    },
    {
      "start": 181.4,
      "end": 185.44,
      "text": "The vast amount of remaining vocabulary odds are condensed here into the other category."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.36,
      "end": 189.28,
      "text": "Temperature reshapes the probabilities used to pick the next token."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.92,
      "end": 191.48,
      "text": "It doesn't change what the model learned."
    },
    {
      "start": 192.28,
      "end": 194.8,
      "text": "As we have seen, the best chance isn't a guarantee."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.8,
      "end": 197.54,
      "text": "Different choices, same learned weights."
    }
  ],
